<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (A bus company has many things to keep track of at the same time: routes, stops, buses, seats, schedules, drivers, conductors, passengers, bookings, cancellations, fares and payments. When this information is kept in registers or spreadsheets, mistakes are easy to make. The most serious mistake is selling the same seat to two passengers on the same trip. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (This project designs and builds a relational database for a Bus Reservation and Fleet Scheduling System. The database is implemented in MySQL, and the important business rules are enforced by the database itself, so they cannot be skipped by mistake. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
