/E (Simple booking programs often check their rules only in application code. If another program or a person edits the data directly, those rules are bypassed. This project places the important rules inside the database, so they hold no matter which front-end is used. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (MySQL 8 was chosen as the database server. From version 8.0.16 it enforces CHECK constraints, which earlier versions accepted but ignored [5]. The front-end is planned in Python, which can talk to MySQL through a connector library and run SQL statements, transactions and reports. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
