/Pg 28 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
633 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (2NF: only route_stop has a composite key, and its only non-key column, stop_order, depends on the whole key \(route_id, stop_id\). All other tables have a single-column key. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
634 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (3NF: no non-key column depends on another non-key column. For example, a trip stores only the ids of its bus, driver and route. The bus type, driver name and cities are stored once in their own tables and are found by joining. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (Three columns need a note. The column active_seat in booking is calculated by the database from seat_id and status; it is not typed in by users, so it cannot become inconsistent, and it exists only to enforce the booking rule. The column refund_amount in cancellation is computed by a trigger and stored as a record of what was refunded. The column total_seats in bus records the declared capacity of the bus; it is not automatically compared with the number of rows in seat \(see Section 5.2\). )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
