965 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 208 0 R
/T (A simple UNIQUE \(trip_id, seat_id\) constraint would stop double booking, but it would also stop a cancelled seat from being sold again, because the cancelled row would still exist. To solve this, the booking table has a generated column active_seat, which equals seat_id while the booking is Confirmed and is NULL when it is Cancelled. The constraint UNIQUE \(trip_id, active_seat\) ignores NULL values, so a seat can have many cancelled bookings but only one confirmed booking on a trip. )
/E (A simple UNIQUE \(trip_id, seat_id\) constraint would stop double booking, but it would also stop a cancelled seat from being sold again, because the cancelled row would still exist. To solve this, the booking table has a generated column active_seat, which equals seat_id while the booking is Confirmed and is NULL when it is Cancelled. The constraint UNIQUE \(trip_id, active_seat\) ignores NULL values, so a seat can have many cancelled bookings but only one confirmed booking on a trip. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
