2864 0 obj
<<
/Title (A simple UNIQUE \(trip_id, seat_id\) constraint would stop double booking, but it would also stop a cancelled seat from being sold again, because the cancelled row would still exist. To solve this, the booking table has a generated column active_seat, which equals seat_id while the booking is Confirmed and is NULL when it is Cancelled. The constraint UNIQUE \(trip_id, active_seat\) ignores NULL values, so a seat can have many cancelled bookings but only one confirmed booking on a trip.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2859 0 R
>>
endobj
